}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/networks/tpl-MNI152NLin2009c_atlas-DesikanKilliany_desc-MEGAlpha_dscalar",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description" : [ {
    "@value" : "Per-region MEG alpha-band amplitude values aligned with the 68 cortical parcels\nof the Desikan-Killiany atlas. Sourced from\ntvb-ontology-optim-workshop/notebooks/data/{lh,rh}_megalpha_parc.csv.\n\nThe measure exhibits the canonical cortical-hierarchy gradient:\n  - unimodal sensory regions (pericalcarine, cuneus, lateraloccipital,\n    transversetemporal) score high  (~0.40)\n  - transmodal regions       (rostralanteriorcingulate, frontalpole,\n    temporalpole, medialorbitofrontal) score low (~0.15)\n\nUsed as a per-region cortical-gradient signal in experiments that need\nto ground a hierarchy (e.g. reservoir-computing frequency-gradient\ntargets, JR-MEG peak-frequency optimisation). The values are\ndimensionless normalised amplitudes; downstream consumers rescale\nto a task-appropriate range (e.g. omega in Hz).\n"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/Network"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "tpl-MNI152NLin2009c_atlas-DesikanKilliany_desc-MEGAlpha_dscalar"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "Desikan-Killiany 68 cortical parcels with MEG alpha amplitudes per region"
  } ]
}, {
